<b>יג.</b> "Voluntary" - from the Mechaber it appears one should not say "Yehi ratzon" after chatat or asham, since they are not voluntary; even asham talui is treated strictly in YD 5. Bach and Nachalat Tzvi in the name of Maharshal allow a conditional formula after both chatat and asham; Magen Avraham and Taz challenge this. Magen Avraham concludes: after asham one may say, "If I became liable for asham..." (since asham does not require prior knowledge), but after chatat one should say nothing. Other authorities sided with Maharshal and permit even chatat conditionally: "If I became liable... and if not, it is Torah study." On Shabbat and Yom Tov do not say "Yehi ratzon"; reading passages as Torah is fine. Some write not to say other offerings either even as Torah reading; this is debated.
